'''Braziers''' can be found within the [[ice demon]] room during the [[Chambers of Xeric]]. Players must fill and light the braziers with [[kindling (Chambers of Xeric)|kindling]], obtained from nearby [[sapling (Chambers of Xeric)|trees]], to defrost the ice demon in order to fight it. The rate that the ice demon will defrost is determined by the amount of kindling burning in the room. Once the ice demon is defeated, players may progress to the next room.

The braziers will burn on a timer, dependent on the amount of kindling fuelling it, and weighted by the players in the raid. Each kindling lit in the brazier gives 36 points for the raid, and lighting the brazier gives 32 points.

A player's [[Firemaking]] level affects their chance of successfully lighting a brazier. This uses the standard Firemaking skill roll, with an 8% success chance at level 1, scaling linearly to 78% at level 99. Failed attempts do not light the brazier, requiring the player to try again.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1527317975521300510|date=16 July 2026|quote=Yes - it's a normal skill-roll, using 8% success at level 1 and scaling up linearly to 78% at level 99.|ctxquote=Hello Ash, 2 more question regarding Ice Demon braziers: Does Firemaking level affect a successful lighting chance? What is the failure rate on lighting a brazier?
}}

